The rest of the lineup, including updated <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/16/ipad-12-release-date/">entry-level iPad, mid-level iPad Air,</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/01/apple-ipad-pro-spring-2027/">high-end iPad Pro</a> models, should follow in the first half of 2027. Gurman says Apple is also working on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/12/two-new-apple-pencils-next-year-report/">two new Apple Pencil models</a> to replace the existing lower-end Apple Pencil with USB-C port and higher-end Apple Pencil Pro.<br/>
